= What does Ownership mean?
An organization owner represents the community and is tasked with managing accounts, projects, domains, and related services for the community organization.
Somewhat unsurprisingly, an organization owner has full administrative permissions on the GitHub organization or other related platforms and accounts.

If you have ideas on improving the governance model and reduce the risk of account takeover posing a threat to the community organization assets, please open an #link("https://github.com/typst-community/org/issues/new")[issue].

